{"authored" [{"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b2eb47829254951cefcf35df8e77e4f5c27ee2da0011f92cfa11d7719611da2" "basis" 2000 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b2eb47829254951cefcf35df8e77e4f5c27ee2da0011f92cfa11d7719611da2" "basis" 2000 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316584" "field" nil "attribute" "questi