r-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/state.json" "file_sha256" "951272036a9a84b190a992e32fe486e55947e740c8692d517e31cb836257c4b4" "basis" 1373 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(5,2),(4,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b8fbb74fd01f03fbb679e8c8e9048784eb4bdd08fe43541eb64b009ef4dd7f4" "basis" 2115 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/aef99dd5276166e5c7b4fb2f716b060390b6577f2d3625dd5dc835bcec6c4856.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b8fbb74fd01f03fbb679e8c8e9048784eb4bdd08fe43541eb64b009ef4dd7f4" "basis" 2115 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8f12f67c515551308fa247bf9f644c620d693c31d1b5e9f062904df55636ee" "basis" 2115 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b8fbb74fd01f03fbb679e8c8e9048784eb4bdd08fe43541eb64b009ef4dd7f4" "basis" 2115 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "4b8fbb74fd01f03fbb679e8c8e9048784eb4bdd08fe43541eb64b009ef4dd7f4" "basis" 2115 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"ques