cademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316597" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8aae5faf2b7bd1510d0c5f4e1c2be76a744f8381f4c9fd14bd436ef501dbac62"} {"question" "q-316597" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316597" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot 2=30-8=22.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,22\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8aae5faf2b7bd1510d0c5f4e1c2be76a744f8381f4c9fd14bd436ef501dbac62"} {"question" "q-316599" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316599" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/state.json" "file_sha256" "84a3e3a622891b5c52e733c8afb9f59eead4747f9f907a332539350369c921f8"} {"question" "q-316602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end